    "Why Cheaper Oil Hasn't Fixed Diesel Prices",
    "Crude oil and diesel are connected commodities, but their prices do not always move together.",
    "Refineries must process crude into usable products, including gasoline, diesel, jet fuel and heating oil. When refining capacity is disrupted, the availability of those products can remain limited even as crude supplies improve.",
    "An Allianz Research report published November 13 estimated that disruptions affecting Middle Eastern and Russian energy infrastructure had taken approximately 3.5 million barrels per day of refining capacity offline.",
    "The resulting shortage has increased the premium buyers pay for refined fuels relative to crude oil.",
    "Restoring tanker shipments alone will not eliminate that premium. Damaged facilities must return to service, export restrictions must ease and depleted inventories must be replenished.",
    "America's Diesel Inventory Problem",
    "The United States possesses substantial domestic refining capacity, but American producers have also been supplying international markets affected by the shortage.",
    "The International Road Transport Union reported that American distillate inventories fell below 100 million barrels at the end of October, their lowest level since 2003.",
    "Inventories subsequently recovered to approximately 103 million barrels, but the decline illustrates the pressure on domestic fuel supplies.",
    "American refiners must balance domestic consumption against overseas demand while maintaining equipment and managing seasonal changes in production.",
    "Low inventories leave less room to absorb unexpected refinery outages or another disruption to international energy shipments.",
    "Europe Faces an Even More Complicated Recovery",
    "European diesel markets remain exposed to disruptions in both Russia and the Middle East.",
    "According to International Energy Agency figures reported by Euronews, European wholesale diesel prices remained approximately 77% above pre-war levels despite a substantial retreat in crude oil prices.",
    "Russia's refining industry continues to face Ukrainian attacks, while Middle Eastern fuel exports have recovered more slowly than crude shipments.",
    "European countries have responded through emergency inventory releases, temporary tax reductions and other measures intended to protect consumers and transportation companies.",
    "Those policies can provide immediate relief, but they cannot permanently replace lost refining capacity.",
    "The Cost Reaches Beyond the Fuel Pump",
    "Diesel powers much of the infrastructure responsible for moving goods through the American economy.",
    "Trucking companies, agricultural producers, construction contractors, railroads and industrial operators depend on it.",
    "Consider a commercial truck averaging seven miles per gallon and traveling 100,000 miles annually.",
    "At $6 per gallon, its annual fuel expense would approach $85,700. At $4 per gallon, the same operation would spend approximately $57,100.",
